  "final_message": "I have initiated the listing of files in the project and will review the output shortly.\nI will check the command execution results once complete.\nI will check the search results once the task completes.\nI am checking the git log for context.\nI am searching for all references to `channel` across `src` and `test`.\nI will check the git output once completed.\nI cannot remove `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/GEMINI.md#L27).\n\n### Architecture Conflict\n- **ARCH-4 Requirement**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Changes must be additive, must not break deployed consumers, and renames/removals must go through deprecation.\n- **Breaking Change**: Removing `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) schema breaks deployed consumers expecting `OrderPlaced` (v3).\n- **Domain Dependency**: The [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) factory derives `channel` directly from [`Order.channel`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L23). Removing it from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model would prevent the service from populating the event.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\nTo retire `channel` in compliance with ARCH-4:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L16) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L23).\n2. Announce deprecation and coordinate with downstream consumer teams (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`).\n3. Prepare a schema version migration (e.g. `OrderPlaced` v4) before completely dropping the field.\n\nWould you like to proceed with marking `channel` as deprecated across the domain model and event definitions?\n",
